Hi Harlan,

It works for me:

> library(plyr)

> dd <- data.frame(x=c('a','a'), y=as.Date(c('2010-01-01', '2010-02-02')), z=c(1,2))
> ddply(dd, .(x), function(q) {q})

  x          y z
1 a 2010-01-01 1
2 a 2010-02-02 2

Hadley

PS.  You can use the identity function instead of creating your own,
and this is what plyr does but default if you omit that argument.

