Got it! Thanks again. You have created some wonderful functions, Hadley.

So, here is what I did specifically:

# Lays out the replications in a data.frame:
aa <- rdply(2,  cat_sum1(datas,datas$mod2),.progress = "tk")

# This function will then output the mean values for each variable
over x number of replications:
 ddply(aa,  .(mod),  summarize, mean(r),mean(n) ,mean(z),
+  mean(var.z), mean(wi))

  mod mean.r. mean.n.   mean.z. mean.var.z. mean.wi.
1   1   0.482    26.0 0.5434789  0.06114350     23.0
2   2   0.288    36.2 0.3105072  0.07328868     33.2
3   3   0.304    22.4 0.3287110  0.07234700     19.4
4   4   0.382    33.4 0.4203965  0.04931122     30.4

This is really wonderful. Thanks again.

AC

